- description: Kubernetes operator secret-leak queries, plus the coverage diagnostic

- queries: .

# The two security queries. Both conditions in this block are ANDed, so a
# `problem`/`path-problem` query without the `security` tag is still excluded.
- include:
    kind:
      - problem
      - path-problem
    tags contain: security

# The coverage diagnostic. This has to be a *separate* include block rather than
# another entry under the block above: conditions inside one block are ANDed, so
# adding `diagnostic` to the `kind` list there would have required a diagnostic
# query to also carry `tags contain: security`, and relaxing the tag condition to
# admit it would have widened the first block for the security queries too.
# Separate blocks are ORed, so this adds the diagnostic and changes nothing else.
#
# The seven Exploration queries stay out because they carry no query metadata at
# all — no `@kind`, no `@id` — so no `kind:` condition in either block can match
# them. Verify with:
#   codeql resolve queries --search-path=. -- hoeg/k8s-operators
# which must list exactly K8sSecretsLeak.ql, K8sCustomResourceSqlInjection.ql and
# Diagnostics/CustomResourceCoverage.ql.
- include:
    kind: diagnostic
